to a prefiling vexatious litigant order (an order that you cannot file a new case in a California court without first getting permission of the leader of the court), ask the court for permission to file a new document in a California court.\n\n# Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant (VL-110)\n\nIf you are subject to a prefiling vexatious litigant order (an order that you cannot file a new case in a California court without first getting permission of the leader of the court), ask the court for permission to file a new document in a California court.\n\nGet form VL-110\n\nEffective: September 1, 2018--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVexatious Litigant List | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/news-reference/reports-publications/vexatious-litigant-list)\nciteturn1718search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; VL-110, Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious LitigantThis optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. ... If you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.\n\n## Other Requirements and Considerations\n\nThe Judicial Council’s annual dissemination of the vexatious litigant list to court clerks is required. To remove a name from the vexatious litigant list, the council must receive an order directly from the issuing court vacating the prefiling order.\n\nPlease note that if a person has been declared a vexatious litigant, but there is no prefiling order, or if there is an order requiring posting of security but no prefiling order, the name will not appear on the list.\n\n## Forms\n\nVL-100, Prefiling Order—Vexatious Litigant.\nThis mandatory Judicial Council form is to be used by the courts or a party when declaring a person or organization a vexatious litigant requiring a prefiling order.\n\nVL-110, Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant\nThis optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1718search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * UD-116 Declaration for Default Judgment by Court (Unlawful Detainer—Civ. ...   * VL-110 Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * VL-110 Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * VL-115 Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * VL-120 Application for Order to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner From Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * VL-125 Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n## [Button: Wage Garnishment]\n\n  * WG-001 * Application for Earnings Withholding Order Effective: July 1, 2012\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * WG-002 * Earnings Withholding Order Effective: January 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * WG-003 * Employee Instructions Effective: January 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPENDIX A (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files?file=file%2Fappendix.pdf)\nciteturn1718search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Crawled: 7 mont